 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Spherical Harmonics Rotation](3985-spherical-harmonics-rotation.md)
-Spherical Harmonics Rotation computes the new SH coefficients of a function after rotating the viewing coordinate system by $\pm \pi/2$ around the X-axis. It sets itself apart from general rotation methods by using precomputed analytic tables for specific $\pm 90^\circ$ rotations, avoiding expensive matrix multiplications or numerical integration. It is used when the Gaussian splat's orientation changes relative to the camera, requiring the SH coefficients to be transformed to maintain view-dependent consistency.
+Spherical Harmonics Rotation computes the new SH coefficients of a function after rotating the viewing coordinate system by $\pm \pi/2$ around the X-axis. It sets itself apart from general rotation methods by using precomputed analytic tables for specific $\pm 90^\circ$ rotations, avoiding expensive matrix multiplications or numerical integration. Choose it when the Gaussian splat's orientation changes relative to the camera, requiring the SH coefficients to be transformed to maintain view-dependent consistency.
 
 ### [Spherical Harmonics Encoder](4390-spherical-harmonics-encoder.md)
-A neural network module that encodes a 3D direction vector into spherical harmonics (SH) coefficients up to a specified degree. It solves the problem of representing directional information (view direction) in a differentiable, basis-function expansion for view-dependent rendering. It differs from [Spherical Harmonics Evaluation](3848-spherical-harmonics-evaluation.md) by providing the raw basis coefficients rather than the final RGB color, and from [Neural Basis Functions](19516-neural-basis-functions.md) by relying on standard orthogonal polynomial bases rather than custom analytic forms.
+A neural network module that encodes a 3D direction vector into spherical harmonics (SH) coefficients up to a specified degree. It solves the problem of representing directional information (view direction) in a differentiable, basis-function expansion for view-dependent rendering. Choose it when a differentiable basis-function expansion is required rather than direct RGB evaluation.
 
 ### [Spherical Harmonics Data Extraction](6960-spherical-harmonics-data-extraction.md)
-Spherical Harmonics (SH) Data Extraction parses SH coefficients from a 3D Gaussian Splatting model file (typically a PLY format) into a structured data layout suitable for GPU rendering. It solves the problem of mapping flat, property-based storage in the source file to the hierarchical texture arrays required by the rendering engine. It is distinct from [Spherical Harmonics Evaluation](3848-spherical-harmonics-evaluation.md), which computes color from these coefficients, and [Spherical Harmonics Rotation](3985-spherical-harmonics-rotation.md), which transforms them for view-dependent effects.
